course: dictionary
lesson: 5206
title: Japan, the country
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Japan is the name of a country, so it always starts with a capital letter: Japan. It is an island country in East Asia, in the Pacific Ocean, and its capital city is Tokyo. Japanese is the word for things from Japan, such as the language and the people.
explain: Context tells you which meaning is meant. «Bon Odori is a calm circle dance at Japan's summer Obon festival.» Japan's shows that the festival belongs to the country. Ask yourself: is this word naming a place, or describing something?
explain: Some words look the same but mean different things. A capital-letter Japan is a country. A small-letter japan is a hard, glossy black varnish. Check the sentence around the word, then try your meaning in it to see if it makes sense.
fact: Japan is an island country in East Asia, in the Pacific Ocean.
fact: The capital city of Japan is Tokyo.
fact: «Japanese» means from Japan, or the language of Japan.
fact: «Japan» with a small j means a hard, glossy black varnish, and to coat something with it.
fact: «Fugu» is the Japanese name for pufferfish, which can be poisonous unless they are prepared by a licensed chef.
exercise: «Bon Odori is a calm circle dance at Japan's summer Obon festival.» In which country is this festival held? | Russia | Australia | China | *Japan
exercise: What is the capital city of Japan? | Kyoto | *Tokyo | Beijing | Osaka
exercise: Which word means from Japan, as in the language of Japan? | Tokyo | Islander | Pacific | *Japanese
test: In the sentence «Japan, which had modernised fast, defeated Qing China», what is Japan? | A kind of owl | A varnish | *A country | A festival
test: What does a small-letter japan mean? | A type of pufferfish | A circle dance | *A hard, glossy black varnish | An island in the Pacific Ocean
exam: Which sentence uses Japan as the name of a country? | *«The Nationalists fought Japan in a big war.» | «The dance was calm and slow.» | «The owl nests in old hollow trees.» | «The box had a hard, shiny japan coat.»
